## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- A15 / B17 and the U+200B verdict lines. The zero-width lines and the Q16–Q20 body paragraphs match the Korean source. Deleting them, or turning Q16–Q20 into headings, fails the blocks and heading checks. They are source layout, not disposable Portuguese blank lines.
- A26. The linked page is article 3, and the label already says so. The Korean anchor text is still article 10 of the business-tax act, and that digit has to remain in the Portuguese label. The URL was not changed.
- A14’s “ultrapassar 1 pessoa”. That figure is the statutory threshold of more than one worker, not the “each victim / each accident” wording. Dropping the digit fails the number check.
- 004 “é, pelo contrário, uma parte da sede” was left. It is the ordinary parenthetical “rather”, not the sentence-initial “Pelo contrário” that denies the previous sentence. The six openers were changed.
- “delito” in 003 Q19 (criminal hit-and-run) and in 002 (a criminal analogue of breach of trust) was left. The civil Article 197 claim was the one that had to stop saying “delito”.
